{"name":"Scud","hex":"#acd7c8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Scud","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A Soviet-developed tactical ballistic missile."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Scud"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scud missile","blocks":[{"text":"A Scud missile is one of a series of tactical ballistic missiles developed by the Soviet Union during the Cold War. It was exported widely to both Second and Third World countries. The term comes from the NATO reporting name attached to the missile by Western intelligence agencies. The Russian names for the missile are the R-11, and the R-17 Elbrus. The name Scud has been widely used to refer to these missiles and the wide variety of derivative variants developed in other countries based on the Soviet design."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Scud-launcher-England1.jpg/330px-Scud-launcher-England1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scud_missile","wikidata":"Q221641"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/9P117_9K72.jpg/500px-9P117_9K72.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/9P117_9K72.jpg/1280px-9P117_9K72.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/9P117_9K72.jpg/500px-9P117_9K72.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"MAZ-543 (9P117) Launcher with 8K14 rocket of 9K72 missile complex \"Elbrus\" (Scud B), Saint-Petersburg Artillery Museum, Russia. (2007)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A9P117_9K72.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Wz8K14_RB3.jpg/500px-Wz8K14_RB3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail